<%- include('../partials/head') %>
<%- include('../partials/header') %>
<main class="container narrow" id="main" style="padding:1.2rem 0 2.6rem">
  <nav class="breadcrumbs dark"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep">/</span><span class="cur"><%= pageHeading %></span></nav>

  <section class="page-head" style="border-radius:var(--radius);padding:clamp(1.6rem,4vw,3rem);margin-bottom:1.4rem">
    <span class="badge gold">One owner · Fashion only</span>
    <h1 style="color:#fff;margin:.65rem 0 .45rem;font-family:'Playfair Display',Georgia,serif;font-weight:500">The Biahens standard</h1>
    <p class="sub" style="max-width:72ch">Every fashion product on this site is selected and uploaded by the owner. Biahens Enterprise is not an open marketplace and does not accept third-party product listings.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Why we keep one considered collection</h2>
    <p>Open marketplaces can offer endless listings, but it is not always clear who is selling an item or who will help if something goes wrong. Biahens takes a more personal approach: the owner selects the fashion range and is responsible for the products customers see here.</p>
    <p>That focus helps us keep the store about what we know and love — clothing, Ghanaian and African-inspired fashion, shoes, bags and accessories. We want each listing to be clear, each price to be ours and each customer to know exactly who they are buying from.</p>

    <h2>Can I upload or sell products on the website?</h2>
    <p><b>No. Only the Biahens Enterprise owner can upload, publish, price or edit products.</b> Customers and outside sellers cannot create listings. Product management is protected inside the owner control panel, and the restriction is enforced by the website itself.</p>
    <p>If you are a designer, maker or fashion supplier, you are welcome to introduce your collection to us for consideration. A conversation or supplier proposal does not create a public listing: the owner decides what to purchase and what, if anything, is added to the store.</p>

    <h2>Fashion suppliers and local makers</h2>
    <p>We are interested in thoughtful fashion and accessories, including:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Ghanaian-made clothing, contemporary African prints and carefully finished everyday pieces;</li>
      <li>shoes, bags and accessories that fit the Biahens point of view;</li>
      <li>reliable sizing, material and care information; and</li>
      <li>wholesale terms, minimum quantities and a clear restock timeline.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Send a short introduction, product photographs, size or material details and wholesale pricing to <a href="mailto:<%= settings.sales_email %>"><%= settings.sales_email %></a>. We will be in touch if the collection is a fit.</p>

    <div class="inline-alert"><b>For shoppers:</b> your order is always with Biahens Enterprise. No outside seller will contact you to request extra payment or arrange delivery separately.</div>

    <div class="row wrap" style="gap:.6rem;margin-top:1.4rem">
      <a class="btn primary" href="/new-arrivals">Shop the latest edit <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="/contact">Contact Biahens</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>
<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
